# Single-page app rewrite, for Render's static site host.
#
# React Router handles /orders/62 in the browser, but a static host knows nothing about it. Ask
# for that URL directly — a refresh, a bookmark, a pasted link — and the host looks for a file
# at /orders/62, does not find one, and serves its own 404. The app never gets to run.
#
# This rewrites every unmatched path to index.html so the router boots and reads the URL itself.
# 200, not 301: a redirect would change the address bar to / and lose the path that was asked
# for, which is the whole thing being preserved.
#
# Real files win over this rule, so /assets/index-*.js still serves the bundle.
/*  /index.html  200
